Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:03:58 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 36/90] Plutonium: page zoom for tabs

EXO-TAB-FEATURES (docs/features/TAB_FEATURES.md, "Zoom"): the registry's
tabs get Chrome's ZoomController (plutonium_zoom.{h,cc}), with Chrome's
per-site levels in the profile, shared by every thread. The tab's state
reports "zoom" (the percent) and "zoomDefault". Commands zoom-in,
zoom-out and zoom-reset (also Ctrl+plus, Ctrl+minus and Ctrl+0 the page
let through) go through zoom::PageZoom as Chrome's do, and zoom-set
{percent} sets the site's level. Ctrl+wheel arrives as
ContentsZoomChange(), as in BrowserWebContentsDelegate.
